Defensive Security Intro - TryHackMe Lab 

🔐 Completed TryHackMe Lab:- Defensive Security – Intro

Today, I completed the TryHackMe – Defensive Security Intro lab, which provided a strong foundation in how modern security teams detect, monitor, and respond to cyber threats. This room helped me understand how defenders protect infrastructure proactively using tools, frameworks, and real-world workflows.

🧭 🔍 Lab Overview:-

The lab introduces the essential concepts of blue teaming, focusing on:

Threat detection
Log analysis
Monitoring tools
Incident response workflow
Understanding how SOC teams operate

It sets the stage for hands-on defensive skills used in real organizations to protect systems against attacks.

🛠 🧰 Tools Explored:-

During the lab, I worked with:
SIEM (Security Information & Event Management) tools
Endpoint logs (Windows Event Viewer, Sysmon basics)
Network monitoring techniques
Defensive frameworks (MITRE ATT&CK concept introduction)

These tools help analysts detect malicious behavior, investigate indicators, and respond effectively.

🧪 📝 Key Learnings / Walkthrough Summary:-

1)Understanding the SOC Structure:-
Roles such as Tier 1 Analyst, Tier 2 Analyst, and Incident Responder
How alerts are triaged and escalated

2)Log Sources & Their Importance:-
Windows logs and Sysmon data
Key log events to monitor for attacks
Why logs are an analyst’s biggest asset

3)MITRE ATT&CK Framework Basics:-
How to map techniques to adversary behavior
Understanding attacker tactics and defensive moves
4)Introduction to SIEM Concepts:-
How SIEM collects, normalizes, and correlates events
Importance of queries, detection rules, and dashboards

5)Defensive Mindset:-
Thinking like a defender
How detection engineering and monitoring reduce risk

🎯 Key Takeaways:-

✔ Defensive security relies on visibility, and logs provide that visibility.
 ✔ Understanding attacker behavior (MITRE) helps design better detections.
 ✔ SOC analysts play a crucial role in early threat detection and incident response.
 ✔ Tools + mindset = effective blue team defense.

🚀 Moving Forward:-

This was a great foundation toward building real-world SOC & defensive security skills.
 I’m excited to continue exploring hands-on rooms like SOC Level 1, Blueprint, and Security Monitoring to deepen my expertise.
